---
// Who asks whom, and where the caches are: app → stub resolver in the OS → recursive resolver →
// authoritative servers. Every layer on your side keeps its own cache, with its own rules.
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 400 448" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="dns-roles-t dns-roles-d">
  <title id="dns-roles-t">The four roles in a lookup, and their caches</title>
  <desc id="dns-roles-d">
    From top to bottom. Your app, with its runtime's own cache, such as the browser's or the
    JVM's. It calls getaddrinfo, which asks the stub resolver in the operating system, with the
    OS cache. The stub sends one question over UDP port 53, or encrypted with DoH or DoT, to a
    recursive resolver, whose cache is shared by thousands or millions of users. On a miss, the
    recursive resolver asks the authoritative servers in turn: root, TLD and the domain's own.
    Only those authoritative servers hold the truth; every layer above holds copies.
  </desc>
  <defs>
    <marker id="dns-roles-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" style="fill: var(--viz-flow)" />
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <g font-size="19">
    <rect x="4" y="4" width="392" height="62" rx="16" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-client-soft); stroke: var(--viz-client)" />
    <text x="18" y="30" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Your app</text>
    <text x="18" y="54" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">cache: browser, JVM, your own code</text>

    <rect x="4" y="110" width="392" height="62" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-server-soft); stroke: var(--viz-server)" />
    <text x="18" y="136" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Stub resolver (the OS)</text>
    <text x="18" y="160" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">cache: one machine; reads /etc/hosts</text>

    <rect x="4" y="216" width="392" height="62" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-server-soft); stroke: var(--viz-server)" />
    <text x="18" y="242" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Recursive resolver</text>
    <text x="18" y="266" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">cache: shared by many users</text>

    <text x="200" y="438" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">authoritative: no cache, the truth</text>
    <rect x="4" y="354" width="120" height="56" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-store-soft); stroke: var(--viz-store)" />
    <text x="64" y="388" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">root</text>
    <rect x="140" y="354" width="120" height="56" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-store-soft); stroke: var(--viz-store)" />
    <text x="200" y="388" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">TLD</text>
    <rect x="276" y="354" width="120" height="56" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-store-soft); stroke: var(--viz-store)" />
    <text x="336" y="388" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">yours</text>
  </g>

  <g stroke-width="2" style="stroke: var(--viz-flow)" marker-end="url(#dns-roles-arrow)">
    <line x1="60" y1="68" x2="60" y2="106" />
    <line x1="60" y1="174" x2="60" y2="212" />
    <line x1="40" y1="280" x2="40" y2="350" />
    <line x1="140" y1="280" x2="196" y2="350" />
    <line x1="240" y1="280" x2="320" y2="350" />
  </g>
  <g font-size="17" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-flow)">
    <text x="74" y="94" style="font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">getaddrinfo()</text>
    <text x="74" y="200">UDP 53, or DoH / DoT</text>
    <text x="396" y="312" text-anchor="end">on a miss</text>
  </g>
</svg>
